# BodyOps

Personal fitness tracker with AI coaching. Log weight, meals (via phone camera), and workouts. Get daily coaching summaries and progress analytics.

**Stack:** Next.js 14 · FastAPI · Google Sheets (data) · Google Drive (meal photos) · Azure OpenAI · Vercel + Hugging Face Spaces

---

## What you need before starting

| Tool | Version | Get it |
|------|---------|--------|
| Python | 3.12 | python.org |
| Node.js | 20+ | nodejs.org |
| Git | any | git-scm.com |

You also need accounts on:
- **Azure** (for OpenAI / GPT-4o)
- **Google Cloud** (for Sheets + Drive APIs)
- **Vercel** (frontend hosting)
- **Hugging Face** (backend hosting — free, no credit card)

---

## Setup

### 1. Clone and create the virtual environment

```bash
git clone <repo-url>
cd BodyOps

python -m venv .venv

# Windows
.venv\Scripts\activate
# Mac/Linux
source .venv/bin/activate

pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

### 2. Get your Azure OpenAI credentials

1. Go to [portal.azure.com](https://portal.azure.com) → create an **Azure OpenAI** resource
2. Inside the resource: **Keys and Endpoint** → copy `KEY 1` and `Endpoint`
3. Go to **Model deployments** → deploy `gpt-4o` → name the deployment (e.g. `gpt-4o`)

You'll need:
```
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=<KEY 1>
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://<your-resource>.openai.azure.com/
AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4o
AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-08-01-preview
```

### 3. Set up Google Cloud

#### Create project and enable APIs

1. Go to [console.cloud.google.com](https://console.cloud.google.com) → New Project → name it `BodyOps`
2. **APIs & Services → Library** → enable **Google Sheets API** and **Google Drive API**

#### Create a service account

3. **APIs & Services → Credentials → + Create Credentials → Service Account**
4. Name: `bodyops-service` → Create and Continue → Done
5. Click the service account → **Keys → Add Key → Create new key → JSON** → download the file

#### Create an API key (for the Auth Sheet)

6. **Credentials → + Create Credentials → API Key** → copy the key
7. Edit the key → restrict it to **Google Sheets API only**

### 4. Create three Google Spreadsheets

Go to [sheets.google.com](https://sheets.google.com) and create these three spreadsheets:

| Spreadsheet | Share with service account? | Purpose |
|-------------|----------------------------|---------|
| `BodyOps - Data` | Yes (Editor) | All app data |
| `BodyOps - Auth` | **No** | Login credentials |
| `BodyOps - Chat History` | Yes (Editor) | AI chat history |

In **BodyOps - Auth**, set up row 1 as headers and row 2 as your credentials:

| A | B |
|---|---|
| email | password |
| you@example.com | yourpassword |

Copy the spreadsheet ID from each URL: `https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/**<ID>**/edit`

### 5. Create a Google Drive folder for meal photos

1. Go to [drive.google.com](https://drive.google.com) → **New → Folder** → name it `BodyOps Meal Images`
2. Share it with the service account email → **Editor**
3. Open the folder and copy the ID from the URL: `https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/**<ID>**`

### 6. Create `api/.env`

Create the file `api/.env` in the project root and fill in all values:

```env
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=
AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4o
AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-08-01-preview

GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account",...}
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=bodyops-service@<project>.iam.gserviceaccount.com
GOOGLE_SPREADSHEET_ID=
GOOGLE_CHAT_HISTORY_SHEET_ID=
GOOGLE_AUTH_SHEET_ID=
GOOGLE_SHEETS_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID=

JWT_SECRET=
JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
JWT_EXPIRE_MINUTES=10080
```

For `GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON`: open the downloaded JSON file and paste the **entire contents as a single line**.

For `JWT_SECRET`: generate one with:
```bash
python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
```

### 7. Bootstrap Google Sheets

This creates all the required tabs in your spreadsheets:

```bash
python scripts/setup.py
```

Expected output:
```
=== BodyOps Sheet Bootstrap ===

[OK] All required environment variables present

Connecting to Google Sheets...
[OK] Service account authenticated

Main Data Sheet tabs:
  [OK] WeightLogs (created)
  [OK] Meals (created)
  ...

[OK] Bootstrap complete - all tabs ready
```

Run it again any time — it's safe and won't duplicate tabs.

### 8. Run the backend

```bash
uvicorn api.main:app --reload --port 8000
```

Verify it's working: open `http://localhost:8000/health` — should return `{"ok":true,"sheets":true,"drive":true}`

### 9. Run the frontend

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
```

Create `frontend/.env.local`:
```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
```

```bash
npm run dev
```

Open `http://localhost:3000` — log in with the email and password you put in the Auth Sheet.

---

## Deployment

See [SETUP.md](SETUP.md) for full deployment steps.

Quick version:

**Backend → Hugging Face Spaces**
```bash
# 1. Create a write-access token at huggingface.co/settings/tokens
# 2. Add the Space as a remote (include your token for authentication)
git remote add hf https://<username>:<token>@huggingface.co/spaces/<username>/bodyops-api
# 3. Set all env vars in HF Space → Settings → Variables and secrets
# 4. Deploy (--force needed on first push because HF creates an initial commit)
git push hf <your-branch>:main --force
# Subsequent deploys:
git push hf <your-branch>:main
```

**Frontend → Vercel**
```bash
npm install -g vercel   # install CLI once
vercel login            # authenticate in browser

cd frontend
vercel                  # first deploy (preview) — answer prompts: new project, name "bodyops"

# Set the backend URL (replace with your actual HF username):
vercel env add NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL production
# When prompted for value, enter: https://<your-hf-username>-bodyops-api.hf.space

vercel --prod           # production deploy
```

---

## Project structure

```
api/                    FastAPI backend
  main.py               App entry point, CORS, health check
  auth.py               JWT auth, login endpoint
  routers/              Route handlers (weight, meals, workouts, etc.)
  services/             Business logic
  sheets/               Google Sheets client and repo helpers
  agent/                Pydantic AI agent and tools
  models/               Pydantic request/response models

frontend/               Next.js frontend
  src/app/              App Router pages
  src/components/       UI components
  src/lib/api.ts        Typed fetch wrapper (attaches JWT to every request)

scripts/
  setup.py              Google Sheets bootstrap (run once after cloning)
```

---

## Running tests

```bash
pytest tests/
```
